# EduScheduler

Full-stack application that syncs and displays student schedules from a Microsoft 365 educational institution using Microsoft Graph API.

## Architecture
```
Frontend (React + Vite + TS + Tailwind)
  ↕ REST API + JWT
Backend (.NET 10 Web API)
  ↕ Entity Framework Core
SQLite Database
  ↑ Hangfire Background Sync
Microsoft Graph API
```

### Backend Design

- **Clean Architecture**: Controllers → Services → Data (EF Core)
- **SOLID Principles**: Interface-based DI, single-responsibility services
- **Periodic Sync**: Hangfire recurring job fetches users & events from Microsoft Graph and upserts into local SQLite database
- **Security**: JWT Bearer authentication, only essential data exposed via DTOs
- **Batch Processing**: Users synced in batches of 500 with deduplication to handle high volume (253k+ users)

### Frontend Design

- **React Query**: Server state management with caching and automatic refetching
- **Debounced Search**: 300ms debounce on student search to minimize API calls
- **Protected Routes**: JWT-based route protection with automatic redirect
- **Responsive Layout**: Split panel on desktop, stacked on mobile

## Resources Implemented

### Backend (API)
- **JWT Authentication** — Register/Login endpoints with BCrypt password hashing
- **Student List** — Paginated, searchable endpoint (`GET /api/students?search=&page=&pageSize=`)
- **Student Detail** — Get student by ID (`GET /api/students/{id}`)
- **Student Events** — Paginated events per student (`GET /api/students/{id}/events`)
- **Microsoft Graph Sync** — Background service that periodically fetches users and calendar events
- **Manual Sync Trigger** — `POST /api/sync/trigger`
- **Hangfire Dashboard** — Monitor background jobs at `/hangfire` (dev mode)
- **API Documentation** — Scalar API docs at `/scalar/v1`

### Frontend
- Login and Register pages
- Student list with debounced search and pagination
- Event list per student with pagination
- Responsive split-panel layout
- Protected routes with JWT

## Prerequisites

- [.NET 10 SDK](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download/dotnet/10.0)
- [Node.js 24+](https://nodejs.org/)

## How to Run the Project

### Backend
```bash
# From the project root
cd src/EduScheduler.Api

# Restore dependencies
dotnet restore

# Apply database migrations
dotnet ef database update

# Run the API
dotnet run
```

The API will be available at:
- **API**: https://localhost:7186/api
- **Scalar Docs**: https://localhost:7186//scalar/v1
- **Hangfire Dashboard**: https://localhost:7186/hangfire

### Frontend
```bash
# From the project root
cd src/eduschedule-web

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Start dev server
npm run dev
```

The frontend will be available at http://localhost:5173

### Quick Start

1. Start the backend API
2. Register a user via the frontend or `POST /api/auth/register`
3. The Hangfire job will automatically sync Microsoft Graph data every 30 minutes
4. Use `POST /api/sync/trigger` to manually trigger a sync
5. Browse students and their events in the frontend

## How to Run the Tests
```bash
# From the project root
dotnet test

# With verbose output
dotnet test --verbosity normal
```

## Project Structure
```
EduScheduler/
├── EduScheduler.sln
├── README.md
├── src/
│   ├── EduScheduler.Api/          # .NET Backend
│   │   ├── Controllers/           # API endpoints
│   │   ├── Data/                  # EF Core DbContext
│   │   ├── Jobs/                  # Hangfire background jobs
│   │   ├── Models/
│   │   │   ├── Entities/          # Database entities
│   │   │   └── DTOs/              # Data transfer objects
│   │   ├── Services/              # Business logic
│   │   └── Program.cs             # App configuration
│   └── eduschedule-web/           # React Frontend
│       └── src/
│           ├── api/               # Axios client
│           ├── components/        # Reusable UI components
│           ├── hooks/             # Custom React hooks
│           ├── pages/             # Page components
│           └── types/             # TypeScript interfaces
└── tests/
    └── EduScheduler.Tests/        # xUnit unit tests
```

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Description |
|--------|---------|------|-------------|
| POST | `/api/auth/register` | No | Register a new user |
| POST | `/api/auth/login` | No | Login and get JWT token |
| GET | `/api/students` | Yes | List students (paginated, searchable) |
| GET | `/api/students/{id}` | Yes | Get student details |
| GET | `/api/students/{id}/events` | Yes | Get student events (paginated) |
| POST | `/api/sync/trigger` | Yes | Manually trigger Graph sync |

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Backend | .NET, ASP.NET Core Web API |
| Database | SQLite + Entity Framework Core |
| Auth | JWT Bearer + BCrypt |
| Background Jobs | Hangfire |
| API Docs | Scalar (OpenAPI) |
| Frontend | React + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS |
| State Management | TanStack Query (React Query) |
| HTTP Client | Axios |
| Tests | xUnit + Moq (backend) |